  "scope": "Preserve byte-range decisions while replacing per-byte Python range loops with a cached single-byte regex class. Measure ordinary strings and complete PL4 inspections offline; rerun public WAF fixtures and four-framework integrations.",
  "measurement_notes": "42 operator cases and 3 complete-engine cases, five warm-cache timing samples each. Input hashes, decisions, engine rule IDs and all 14 reconstructed framework traces agree before/after. No HTTP timing, CPU isolation, native engine execution or end-to-end speedup claim. Default CRS, ModSecurity unit corpus, seven GoTestWAF configurations and four-framework integrations rerun; explicitly configured CRS and body-limit integration results retained, not rerun.",
  "known_limits": [
    "PL4 false positives are unchanged. Generated JSON array names differ from the pinned native implementation and produce additional rule alerts; this compatibility gap is recorded but not changed in the performance patch.",
    "Historical malformed-range configuration behavior, four ModSecurity unit failures and other unsupported public fixtures remain.",
    "Scanner passive algorithms unchanged; five public sources retained, live framework passive checks rerun. Active scanner gaps unresolved.",
    "A bounded cache controls retained patterns; cold compilation and adversarial configuration churn were not benchmarked."
  ]
}
